 "remarks": "Welcome to 32 Pine Hill Avenue, set on one of East Norwalk's most coveted tree-lined streets, an easy walk to Calf Pasture Beach. The East Norwalk train station is 2 minutes away and Sono station is under 10. This 4-bedroom, 4.5-bath colonial was fully gutted and rebuilt in 2024 with all-new systems, then refined further with upgraded lighting, custom cabinetry, exterior paint, landscaping, and even potted plants were added to the irrigation. A custom center staircase with a built-in wine closet sets the tone, with white oak floors and recessed lighting throughout. The open kitchen and living area features customized cabinetry, a large waterfall island, a 48\" Wolf range, Sub-Zero column refrigerator and freezer, and a gas fireplace. The first floor also offers a formal dining room with a beverage center, a living room with a wood-burning fireplace, a sun room, and an office. Upstairs, the primary suite has a vaulted ceiling, a private deck overlooking the backyard, showcasing beautiful sunsets and a spa-like bath with a soaking tub. Three more bedrooms share two full baths, plus a dedicated laundry room. The finished lower level adds a large recreation space and a full bath.  Andersen windows, central air, gas heat, public utilities, and a Navien tankless water heater keep costs remarkably low. Outside, the level, professionally landscaped 0.46-acre lot offers a patio and an attached 2-car garage. Beach rights add to the appeal, and the home is truly move-in ready!",
